<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lusaka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lusaka is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>, on a plateau in the south-centre of the country. It grew from a small settlement on the railway line and replaced Livingstone as the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a>, officially from 1935. It became the capital of independent Zambia in 1964 and hosted the exiled headquarters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lusaka.jpg" alt="Lusaka" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthew Grollnek · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown_Lusaka.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
